# Local commits — this repo (multitask-safe)

**Prefer** committing your own finished slices locally in `/opt/yatishara-studio`. Still **never push** unless Dallas explicitly asks.

This **no longer forces** end-of-every-turn commits when other agents are also dirtying the tree. Continuous commit pressure while multitasking caused mid-edit files to get swept into the wrong chat’s commits.

## When to commit

Do it when **all** of these are true:

- The changes are from **this turn / this chat**
- The slice is a coherent unit (or a clear `wip:` checkpoint you own)
- Staging will not include another agent’s in-flight files

Good triggers:

- One UX/UI pass or wizard step polish **you** finished
- One CSS/token pass
- One pane/form/component rewrite
- One bug fix or backend slice that stands alone
- Before a risky restyle, delete, or large rewrite
- After adding/updating a Cursor rule or agent SOP in this repo

Prefer **many tiny commits** over one mega commit when you are the sole owner of the dirty paths. Experimental work you own can still be `wip:` so undo stays in git.

## When to skip

- Working tree has files clearly belonging to **another active chat/agent**
- You only answered a question / left no real edits
- User asked you not to commit / is mid-multitask coordination

Leaving **your** large uncommitted batch when you are the only one editing is still a miss. Leaving **someone else’s** dirt alone is correct.

## Commit nudge hook — opted out here

This repo has `.cursor/no-auto-commit`, so the user-level stop hook will **not** inject `COMMIT REQUIRED` follow-ups for Studio. That opt-out exists specifically so multitasking agents do not fight over the same dirty tree.

If Dallas removes the marker, the hook may return — still only commit **this turn’s** files; leave other chats alone.

## How (when you do commit)

1. `git status` / `git diff` — stage only **your** relevant files
2. Commit with HEREDOC; message = why (1–2 sentences)
3. Never update git config; never `--no-verify` unless asked
4. **Do not push** unless explicitly asked
5. Never force-push to main/master
6. Never commit secrets (`.env`, keys, credentials)

## Conflict resolution

| Rule source | This repo |
|---|---|
| User rule “only commit when asked” | Prefer commit when safe; **do not** force through multitask dirt |
| MercuryOS ask-first | Same spirit when other agents are active |
| Push / force-push / secrets | Still forbidden without ask |

